cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Figeometrica, please cite it using this metadata.
title: Figeometrica — executable theory infrastructure for rhetorical figures
abstract: >-
  A theory-compilation framework that turns classical rhetoric — the world's
  oldest taxonomy of text analysis, ~456 named figures of speech defined only
  in prose — into structured, machine-checkable specifications. Every figure
  becomes a FigureSignature (operation × anchor × grain × repetition, extended
  to a versioned slot lattice); a deterministic matcher produces byte-exact
  evidence; a witness protocol with inverse reconstruction makes every
  definition falsifiable. The dataset ships with an evidence ladder enforced by
  continuous integration: no status is claimed without publicly re-runnable
  proof.
